Certificate/private-key handling

Verify from code whether the runtime wrapper:

* never uses the repository’s reference/local PEM as runtime input;
* reconstructs material only from runtime-retrieved bytes;
* preserves already readable PEM bytes exactly;
* fails closed if flattened material cannot be reconstructed safely;
* validates the X.509 certificate;
* validates the private key;
* confirms the certificate and key form a pair;
* uses pass:clue-probe-not-a-passphrase at every intended OpenSSL probe site;
* handles the owner-confirmed unencrypted private key without prompting;
* fails promptly for an encrypted key instead of opening /dev/tty;
* creates temporary files with restrictive permissions;
* removes temporary files after success, failure, and signals;
* avoids placing private-key material in arguments, logs, reports, or permanent installed configuration.

Do not inspect or test the real key.

